# 0103-build-screen-mode-cool-fast.patch -- the owner: the shader build is slower than before (but the phone is much cooler), and "Close" on the build screen does nothing the chevron does not;
# put a build speed option there instead: "Pause - Mode / Notify me - Cancel". Applies after 0102.
#
# WHY SLOWER: since the field report on the Zelda lag, the build's worker threads lower themselves to utility QoS (crates/ibuilder-pipeline/src/sys/qos.rs): iOS then runs them mostly on the
#   efficiency cores and the UI keeps its priority. Results are the same; only the pace changes.
# FIX:
#   * Build screen (GameBuildViewController, GameAppLibrary.cs): while a build runs the bottom bar is "Pause | Mode" over "Notify me | Cancel"; the primary button ("Close" while running) is
#     hidden while it runs (the chevron at the top still goes back to the library). Paused or ended, the bar is as before (Cancel above Resume, or the game's action alone).
#     "Mode: Cool" (leaf) / "Mode: Fast" (hare) opens a menu "Build mode": Cool "Slower and cooler; the app stays smooth" (default), Fast "Faster and hotter; the app may lag", the one in
#     effect ticked (BuildMode, GameAppField.cs).
#   * The choice is saved as fast_build 0/1 in Documents/gameapp.settings.tsv (GameAppUi.FastBuildOn) and told to a running build (gameapp_set_fast_build -> ibuilder_set_fast_build).
#     Log: "build mode: Fast (...); the shader translation follows now, the other steps from the next build" (or ", from the next build" when no build runs).
#   * Rust (not in this patch: sys/qos.rs, ibuilder-ffi, the shim): every run starts from fast_build; Fast leaves the workers at the chain thread's class (at least QOS_CLASS_DEFAULT), Cool
#     lowers them to utility as before; the translator and SPIRV-Cross callbacks of the shim call ibuilder_qos_follow() before each call, so a worker of a running build moves to the new
#     mode within a shader; other threads (boot, game, live translation) are never touched. The stage log says "worker threads at utility QoS (build mode Cool ...)" or "... (build mode Fast ...)".
#     sys/qos.rs is excluded from the framework id and the shim/FFI are not inputs of it: no game needs a rebuild for this change; no shader output changes.
# VERIFIED (2026-11-22, M1 Pro): every patch 0010-0103 applies in order; compile only (dotnet build -c Release -r ios-arm64 -t:Compile on the last device build's generated project):
#   0 errors, the same warnings per file and code as without 0103. cargo clippy -D warnings (ibuilder-pipeline, ibuilder-ffi): clean; qos tests (a worker follows the mode, other threads are
#   left alone) pass.
# NOT VERIFIED: anything on an iPhone (the menu, the bar's layout on a phone and an iPad, the speed and heat of each mode).
# NEW STRINGS: "Mode: ", "Build mode", "Slower and cooler; the app stays smooth", "Faster and hotter; the app may lag", "build mode: ", "the shader translation follows now",
#   "could not save the build mode: ".
